// S441 reproducer — addendum-3 T6(c): component prop types are not checked at the call site; a wrong-type
// boolean literal reports E-SCOPE-001 instead.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/tut-component-prop-type-unchecked.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: §15 (props) "Prop types SHALL be verified at the call site. A prop value that is not assignable to
//           the declared prop type SHALL be a compile error (E-TYPE-031)." — two E-TYPE-031s here.
// Actual:   exit 1 with ONE error: `error [E-SCOPE-001]: Unquoted identifier `true` in attribute `count` cannot
//           be resolved in the current scope…`. The `count="five"` line is accepted: alone it compiles exit 0
//           and renders `<span data-scrml="Badge" count="five">five </span>`.
<program>
const Badge = <span props={ count: number }>${count}</span>
<Badge count="five"/>
<Badge count=true/>
</program>
